MID_SCXX_06_01_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_001: Admiral Jarcham will be here soon. Now, let's try\nto show the admiral all the respect due him.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_047: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_048: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_049: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_050: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_051: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_053: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_002: He'd better not disrespect you. If the rumors are true,\nhe's not the most upstanding person.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_003: Diego, that's hardly getting off on the right foot...
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_004: Apologies, Priest. I'm Jarcham. Sorry if I kept you\nwaiting. I hear you wanted to see me. What is it? 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_005: Y-yes, I have a request...an unusual one.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_006: You have an important ring that once belonged to\nYu Phas. Would you be willing to part with it?
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_007: Hm. So, you've heard that I'm collecting objects\nconnected to Yu Phas.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_008: Why would you want anything of hers? She's a\ngoddess of death—and a terror, to be sure.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_009: Orchel says she just really wants it. But, wait. You're\ncollecting them too, right?
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_010: So you say. Why, then, do you want it?
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_011: I'll overlook your disrespect toward Yu Phas this\nonce. But why are you collecting her memorabilia?
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_012: That's a little hypocritical. We're after the same\nthings, aren't we?
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_013: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_015: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_016: Quiet—I have my reasons for collecting such\nobjects.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_017: A dread god is what I need for the...dire events\nahead of me.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_018: But you've come a long way to talk. You must\nhave interesting reasons of your own.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_019: You're right. I do. Please, I'd like your help.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_020: No need for all that. Just pay me its true worth.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_021: One billion gold. Yes, I think that will do.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_022: One billion?!
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_023: That's enough to build a palace. Who do you think\nyou are—a king or something?
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_024: Hey, old man! Orchel can't pay that much, and\nneither can I.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_025: Truly? If you intend to refuse us, speak plainly.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_026: That sum seems reasonable enough to me. But I balk\nat lining the pockets of one so vile as you.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_027: *sigh* Saw that coming. I'm tired of men who are\nonly interested in gaining coin.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_028: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_030: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_031: What in the heavens... The ring was MINE to begin\nwith and still you dare...
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_032: Say that again? "Mine"? Then you're no priest\nfrom our temples!
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_033: Ahh, n-no, you misunderstand me...
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_034: You're from that estate—the one I stole it from!\nWell, it's mine now. That's that!
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_035: What? You stole it?
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_036: So, the rumors are true. You're working with bandits\non the sly, having them steal for you.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_037: So this old guy's pretending to be important, when\nreally he's just...bad.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_038: Ah. You stole it. So shall we. Now.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_039: Nothing more than a common rogue, then.\nHow predictably dull.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_040: I knew this man was just a worthless crook.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_041: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_043: 
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_044: Shut up! Guess I'll need to make sure this stops\nright here!
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_045: Orchel, I'll report this to Father Nomved. Don't you\nworry about me. I won't get myself caught.
MID_SCXX_06_01_m01_046: Yes, good! I'll stay here with these people and make\nsure Admiral Jarcham gets what he deserves.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m01_001: Get out here, you rogues! Don't let anyone in this\ncrew escape. Kill them all!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m01_002: You have earned my fury—and that's not easy\nto do! You won't get away with this!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m02_001: I'm sorry for dragging you into something so\ndangerous.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m02_002: Don't worry about it. If anyone should have\nYu Phas's item, it should be you.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m02_003: Oh, Cai... Heh. Thank you.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m03_001: I'm sorry I got you into such a dangerous situation\nhere, Dietrich.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m03_002: I do not mind. I lead a dangerous life.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m03_003: Well, I'm glad you don't mind, but I do worry you're\nnot looking after yourself properly.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m04_001: I'm sorry, Theodora. I've gotten you in the middle of\nsuch a dangerous situation.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m04_002: No need for that. I should be thanking you for the\nopportunity to bury this lout myself.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m04_003: I know you're angry that he offended me—I mean,\nYu Phas! But that's no reason to bury him!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m05: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m05_001: I'm sorry, Leda. I didn't mean to drag you into this\nwhole dangerous mess.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m05_002: There's no need to apologize. You did lose to\nBertrand like I asked, so I owe you one anyway.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m05_003: Well, that's not... Ahaha... You really are\na kind person, you know that?
MID_SCXX_06_02_m06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m06_001: I'm sorry, Bertrand. I've put you in the middle of\nsuch a dangerous situation.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m06_002: I'm no stranger to peril. Just keep behind me, alright?
MID_SCXX_06_02_m06_003: Well, I appreciate the offer. Heh. But that's\nnot necessary.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m08_001: I've gotten you in the middle of such a dangerous\nsituation, Anatolia. I'm very sorry.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m08_002: It's clear who is at fault. There's nothing for you to\nworry about here.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m09_001: My place in the afterlife will be guaranteed! Peace\nand rest forever—once I gather enough objects!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m09_002: Yu Phas, please! Be shepherd to my soul!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m09_003: That's why you've done this, despite the risk of piling\non more sins? You don't reach final peace that way!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m09_004: What do YOU know? Tch. I'm going to serve your\nsoul up to Yu Phas on a plate!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m10_001: A-argh!
MID_SCXX_06_02_m10_002: Admiral Jarcham must answer for his sins. The\ntemples will want him alive to face judgment.
MID_SCXX_06_02_m11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_02_m11_001: Phew! We got through it all. Thank you so much\nfor your help!
MID_SCXX_06_e01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e01_001: The admiral has so many people working for him!\nHe's surrounded by guards too.
MID_SCXX_06_e02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e02_001: Is that an {SetColor=Gold}onager{SetColor=Default}? Maybe we can use that to\nbreak up their defensive positions!
MID_SCXX_06_e03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e03_001: She's got her eye on the onager, I bet... Well, that\nlittle fool has a surprise coming to her.
MID_SCXX_06_e03_002: To make it operational, you need to activate {SetColor=Gold}two\nlaunch mechanisms{SetColor=Default}—at the {SetColor=Gold}same time{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SCXX_06_e04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e04_001: Ha! There's no way she can command any sort of\ncomplex maneuver against us!
MID_SCXX_06_e05: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e05_001: Goodness! Does he always bellow everything he\nsays? I heard every word of that.
MID_SCXX_06_e07: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e07_001: Hurry! Let's activate the other one too. That will\nlaunch the rock!
MID_SCXX_06_e09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e09_001: Graaah! Th-they did it? No matter. This is where\nthis all ends!
MID_SCXX_06_e14: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e14_001: Send word to those standing by—ready for our\nambush! We'll teach these fools a lesson.
MID_SCXX_06_e11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e11_001: Oh no! The launch mechanism has reset itself.\nIt's so hard to activate both at once!
MID_SCXX_06_e12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e12_001: Backup troops, get out here! Don't let any of them\nescape with their lives!
MID_SCXX_06_e13: <TH>
MID_SCXX_06_e13_001: The admiral's in a jam. Bad for him. Good for us!\nLet's grab some of this loot and leg it!
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_001: I managed to get my old ring back, Solel...
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_002: I'll always remember the day you gave it to me.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_003: Orchel, I asked the temple folks to take care\nof Jarcham.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_004: Jarcham was like a puppet with its strings cut.\nI rolled him all the way to the temple. 
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_005: Jarcham has been remanded to the temples. Were it\nup to me, he would be drawn and quartered.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_006: I'm back, and Admiral Jarcham's being dealt with\nby the temples. You should be safe now.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_007: 
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_009: 
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_010: Oh, thank you! And to you, Father Nomved.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_011: I took action the moment I heard from Diego. I'm just\nrelieved that you're safe. I also bring good news.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_012: We took possession of every object that Jarcham\nhad—all now in storage at Credna's temple.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_013: Really? That is good news. But why was he so\ndriven to collect them?
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_014: He'd been thieving and doing criminal deals for a\nlong time. A bold, brazen man, and yet a coward.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_015: He'd grown afraid that his crimes were sins that\nwould catch up with him after he died.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_016: So that's why the old guy was collecting things\nrelated to Yu Phas?
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_017: He sought peace after death. He hoped his trinkets\nwould bring it.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_018: Ah. So in his own strange way, he was seeking\nYu Phas's grace.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_019: I see... So he turned to Yu Phas, the goddess of\ndeath, to save himself. How selfish.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_020: 
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_022: 
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_023: Oh... If only he'd had the proper guidance...
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_024: But wait! If he was worried about his fate, why didn't\nhe just stop doing bad things and turn himself in?
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_025: That's a good question, Orchel.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_026: I cannot say. A life led in terror of death holds\nno meaning.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_027: A fair question. His justification amounts to little\nmore than a paltry excuse.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_028: It seems like he was scared of changing himself—\nso he was backed into a corner.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_029: 
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_031: 
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_032: Well, regardless, I am very grateful for your help.\nI'd like to thank you with this.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_034: Again, thanks—and please always let me know if\nthere's anything I can do to help you.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_035: Diego... You can stop hiding. Really, you should\nhave come out and thanked them.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_036: I didn't see the point. I could hear perfectly well\nwhere I was.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_037: You should try to get along with others a little more.\nAnd...I'm sure we can trust that person.
MID_SCXX_06_03_m01_038: Heh. You know me. I'll always be happy enough if\nI can stand watch at your side.